@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Privacy policy for The Slow Road Armenia travel guide.";
}

<section class="page-header">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
        <p>Last updated: November 2026</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow prose">
        <p>The Slow Road Armenia is a free information site. We keep things simple, and that includes your privacy. There are no accounts, no contact forms, no comments and no adverts, and we sell nothing.</p>

        <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
        <p>We use Google Analytics to see how many people read the guide and which pages they find useful. It records the page you opened, roughly where you are (country or city level, never your exact address), the kind of device and browser you use, and which site or search sent you here. It stores a cookie in your browser so that a returning reader is not counted twice. Your full IP address is not stored by Google Analytics.</p>
        <p>We see only totals and trends — we cannot tell who you are, and we measure nothing beyond the page view. The numbers are used for one thing: deciding what to write next.</p>
        <p>Google processes this data on our behalf; see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google's privacy policy</a>. We share it with nobody else, and we run no advertising or remarketing.</p>
        <p>If you would rather not be counted, you can install <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google's opt-out browser add-on</a>, turn on your browser's "Do Not Track" or tracking protection, or block cookies for this site. Nothing on the guide stops working if you do.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>Google Analytics sets its own cookie, as described above. Apart from that, the site keeps one small value in your own browser's storage — your light-or-dark choice, if you press the theme button in the header. It stays on your device and is never sent to us.</p>

        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>If you write to us at <a href="mailto:slowroadarmenia@gmail.com">slowroadarmenia@gmail.com</a>, we use your message only to reply to you. We never share your address.</p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>Links to other websites (for example official visa or exchange-rate pages) are provided for convenience. Those sites have their own privacy policies.</p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>Like any web server, our host keeps standard technical logs (such as IP address and pages requested) for security and troubleshooting.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>If you want to know what we hold about you, or want it deleted, write to the address above and we will help.</p>

        <p><a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">&larr; Back to the guide</a></p>
    </div>
</section>
